## Desired MVP behavior

The application should work as follows:

1. Authentication remains mandatory.
2. After successful registration/login, the user goes to a workspace selection page instead of directly opening the prototype map.
3. The workspace page displays all existing workspaces available in the application.
4. Any authenticated user can open any existing workspace.
5. Opening a workspace navigates to its map and the user starts working with that workspace.
6. Any authenticated user can create a new workspace.
7. A workspace can be deleted manually.
8. There is NO invitation flow.
9. There is NO join code.
10. There is NO explicit "join workspace" action.
11. There is NO private-workspace/access-control model in this MVP.
12. Do not add unnecessary roles/permissions unless the existing implementation makes them unavoidable.

Conceptually:

Unauthenticated
    ↓
/auth
    ↓
Login / Register
    ↓
/workspaces
    ↓
List all workspaces
    ├── Create Workspace
    └── Open Workspace
            ↓
      /workspaces/{workspaceId}/map
            ↓
      existing Area / History / Presence / WebSocket functionality

The workspace is simply the project/map context selected by the authenticated user.

