1. Current-State Architecture

Workspace entity (workspace/Workspace.java)

Fields: id UUID, name VARCHAR(255), createdBy User (FK lazy), createdAt Instant.
Constructor: Workspace(String name, User createdBy).

WorkspaceMember entity (workspace/WorkspaceMember.java)

Fields: id UUID, workspace Workspace (FK lazy), user User (FK lazy), role WorkspaceMemberRole (OWNER | EDITOR | VIEWER).
Unique constraint: (workspace_id, user_id).

WorkspaceRepository / WorkspaceMemberRepository

Both are plain JpaRepository<T, UUID> — no custom queries. No WorkspaceService exists.

DB constraints (V2__core_schema.sql)

fk_workspace_created_by  → users(id) ON DELETE RESTRICT
fk_workspace_member_workspace → workspace(id)          [no CASCADE]
fk_workspace_member_user      → users(id)               [no CASCADE]
fk_area_workspace             → workspace(id)           [no CASCADE]
fk_area_version_area          → area(id)                [no CASCADE]
No ON DELETE CASCADE anywhere. Physical deletion of a workspace requires explicit child cleanup in the correct order: area_version → area → workspace_member → workspace.

AreaService authorization

workspaceId is validated by workspaceRepository.findById() (throws WorkspaceNotFoundException) and used as a WHERE clause scope in all SQL. No WorkspaceMember check exists anywhere in AreaService. Any authenticated user can read or mutate any workspace.

