5. Presence — Current Design and Required Changes

Current design

PresenceService maintains three ConcurrentHashMaps:
- userSessions — userId → Set of sessionIds (all users, all workspaces)
- sessionToUser — sessionId → userId
- userNames — userId → display name

getActiveUsers() returns all globally connected users, regardless of which workspace they are in.

broadcast() always sends to /topic/workspace/{prototypeId}/presence — hardcoded.

PresenceController.getPresence() rejects any workspaceId ≠ prototype, so callers can never get presence for a different workspace.

What must change

Problem: Presence must be per-workspace. Users in workspace A must not appear in workspace B's presence list.

Solution: Track workspaceId per session.

1. Frontend: Pass workspace-id in the STOMP CONNECT headers (alongside Authorization: Bearer).
2. JwtChannelInterceptor: Extract workspace-id from native CONNECT headers; store it in accessor.getSessionAttributes().put("workspaceId", workspaceId). Handle missing/invalid gracefully (log, reject connect or use null).
3. PresenceService.onSessionConnected(): Read workspaceId from StompHeaderAccessor.wrap(event.getMessage()).getSessionAttributes(). Store in a new sessionToWorkspace: ConcurrentHashMap<String, String>.
4. PresenceService.broadcast(): Use sessionToWorkspace.get(sessionId) to determine the workspace topic.
5. PresenceService.getActiveUsers(UUID workspaceId): Filter userSessions to users whose sessions include at least one in the given workspace.
6. PresenceController.getPresence(): Remove prototype guard; validate workspace exists in DB; call presenceService.getActiveUsers(workspaceId).

