9. WorkspaceMember Recommendation

Recommendation: Option B — keep the table in the schema, stop creating entries from register(). Create one OWNER entry when a workspace is created.

Rationale:
- Removing the table requires a Flyway migration (V3), JPA entity deletion, and changes to SchemaIntegrationTest.basicEntityCrudRoundTrip() and uniqueWorkspaceMemberConstraintEnforced(). This is purely destructive and adds risk.
- The table is structurally correct, already constrained, and imposes zero runtime cost.
- Creating a WorkspaceMember(OWNER) entry when a workspace is created is natural and sets up the data model correctly for any future membership feature.
- No membership check is added to Area operations — this is consistent with the MVP goal ("any authenticated user can open any workspace").

The AuthService.register() change: remove WorkspaceMember creation entirely. WorkspaceMember is only created in WorkspaceService.createWorkspace().

